          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The definition of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            effectively enforces an ordering on the “0-faces” – the source and target
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} objects
            – of every 1-cell (every
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi f
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \stackrel{f}{\to} b
            in the category as a morphism from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            instead.
          %p
            But there are many categories for which this is not the case, where every morphism naturally only comes with the information of an unordered pair
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{a,b \}
            of objects, without any prejudice on which is to be regarded as the source and which as the target. An important general example is:
          %ul
            %li
              the category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spans
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spans(C)
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/span"} spans
              in a category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              with pullbacks, or
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality"} dually
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CoSpans
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CoSpans(C)
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cospan"} cospans
              in a category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              with pushouts.
          %p More concrete examples are:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                categories of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism"} cobordisms
                (but notice that cobordisms are naturally regarded as
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cospan"} cospans
                making this a special case of the above example);
            %li
              %p
                the category
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilb"} Hilb
                of Hilbert spaces, where for every linear map
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mi H
                        %mn 1
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi H
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : H_1 \to H_2
                we also have the adjoint map (in the sense of Hilbert spaces, not in the categorical sense)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo †
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mi H
                        %mn 2
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi H
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^\dagger : H_2 \to H_1
                (but notice that, according to
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoidification"} groupoidification
          %p
            A
            %em dagger structure
            on a category is an extra structure which encodes the idea of
            %em removing
            the ordering information on the 0-faces of 1-cells in a category. It is a contravariant functor which sends every morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi a
                  %mo →
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : a \to b
            to a morphism going the other way,
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo †
                    %mo :
                    %mi b
                    %mo →
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^\dagger : b \to a
          %p
            The notation and terminology here is motivated by the example
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilb"} Hilb
            of Hilbert spaces, where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo †
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^\dagger
            is traditionally the adjoint of a linear map
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilb"} Hilb
            and on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nCob"} nCob
            is crucial in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FQFT"} quantum field theory
            where it is used to encode the idea of
            = succeed ":" do
              %strong unitarity
          %p
            a
            %em unitary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FQFT"} functorial QFT
            of dimension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            is supposed to be a functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mi Cob
                  %mo →
                  %mi Hilb
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n Cob \to Hilb
            which respects the †-structure on both sides.
          %h2#terminology Terminology
          %p
            In Wikipedia, a
            %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dagger_category"} dagger category
            is said to be the same as an
            %em involutive category
            or a
            = succeed "." do
              %em category with involution
            %a{:href => "https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Category_with_involution"} Springer’s Encyclopedia of Mathematics
            requires that a “category with involution” is also compatibly
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/posets"} posets
          %p
            In enriched category theory, involutive categories have also been called
            = succeed "." do
              %strong symmetric categories
            %em equality
            rather than an
            = succeed "." do
              %em isomorphism
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horizontal+categorification"} horizontal categorification
            = succeed "," do
              %strong commutative categories
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+monoid"} commutative monoid
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#dagger_categories Dagger categories
          %h4#with_a_family_of_functions With a family of functions
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong dagger category
              or
              = succeed "-category" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo †
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \dagger
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              with a function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo †
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^\dagger: Hom_C(A,B) \to Hom_C(B,A)
              for every object
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi B
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Ob
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A,B \in Ob(C)
            %ul
              %li
                for every
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi Ob
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in Ob(C)
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mn 1
                          %mi A
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo †
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mn 1
                          %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (1_A)^\dagger = 1_A
              %li
                for every
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi B
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Ob
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A,B \in Ob(C)
                and every
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi Hom
                        %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \in Hom_C(A,B)
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi Hom
                          %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi B
                        %mo ,
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \in Hom_C(B,C)
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi g
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi f
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo †
                        %mo =
                        %msup
                          %mi f
                          %mo †
                        %mo ∘
                        %msup
                          %mi g
                          %mo †
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (g \circ f)^\dagger = f^\dagger \circ g^\dagger
              %li
                and for every
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi B
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Ob
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A,B \in Ob(C)
                and every
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi Hom
                          %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo ,
                        %mi B
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \in Hom_C(A,B)
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi f
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo †
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo †
                        %mo =
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ((f)^\dagger)^\dagger = f
            %p
          %h4#with_a_function With a function
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              Given a category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              with a type or class of objects
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ob
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ob(C)
              and a set of morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Mor
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mor(C)
              with source and target functions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mo :
                    %mi Mor
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Ob
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s:Mor(C) \to Ob(C)
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi t
                      %mo :
                      %mi Mor
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi Ob
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t:Mor(C) \to Ob(C)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is a
              %strong dagger category
              if it has a function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo †
                    %mo :
                    %mi Mor
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Mor
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^\dagger:Mor(C) \to Mor(C)
              such that
            %ul
              %li
                for every term
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo :
                        %mi Mor
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:Mor(C)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi t
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo †
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s(f) = t(f^\dagger)
              %li
                for every term
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo :
                        %mi Mor
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:Mor(C)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi t
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi s
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo †
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t(f) = s(f^\dagger)
              %li
                for every term
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo :
                        %mi Mor
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:Mor(C)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo †
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo †
                      %mo =
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f^\dagger)^\dagger = f
              %li
                for every term
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo :
                        %mi Ob
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a:Ob(C)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi id
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo †
                      %mo =
                      %mi id
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} id(a)^\dagger = id(a)
              %li
                for every term
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi Mor
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:Mor(C)
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mo :
                      %mi Mor
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g:Mor(C)
                such that
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi t
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %msub
                          %mo =
                          %mi D
                        %mi s
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi g
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t(f) =_D s(g)
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi g
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi f
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo †
                        %mo =
                        %msup
                          %mi f
                          %mo †
                        %mo ∘
                        %msup
                          %mi g
                          %mo †
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (g \circ f)^\dagger = f^\dagger \circ g^\dagger
            %p
          %h4#with_a_functor With a functor
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong dagger category
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              equipped with a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contravariant+functor"} contravariant endofunctor
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
              from the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^{op}
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              itself
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo †
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\dagger : C^{op} \to C
            %p which
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  is the
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity-on-objects"} identity-on-objects
              %li
                %p
                  is an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/involution"} involution
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mo †
                            %mi op
                          %mo ∘
                          %mo †
                          %mo =
                          %msub
                            %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} id
                            %mi C
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \dagger^{op} \circ \dagger = \mathrm{id}_C
            %p
          %p
            This definition, which is perhaps the most concise, does rely on a notion of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity-on-objects+functor"} identity-on-objects functor
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principle+of+equivalence"} principle of equivalence
            (except for
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+categories"} strict categories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            (or more generally
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intensional+type+theory"} intensional type theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity-on-objects+functor"} identity-on-objects functor
            for details. When unwound for
            = succeed "-categories," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo †
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \dagger
          %h3#special_morphisms Special morphisms
          .un_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              A morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              in a †-category is called a
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+morphism"} unitary morphism
              if its †-adjoint equals its
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse"} inverse
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo †
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f^\dagger = f^{-1}
                    \\,.
          %p
            For the purpose of considering what makes two objects of a
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo †
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \dagger
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalent
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphisms
            (invertible morphisms) but rather all unitary isomorphisms.
          %p
            The unitary isomorphisms form a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
            %em
              dagger-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/core"} core
            of the
            = succeed "-category." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo †
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \dagger
          %p
            For example, in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilb"} Hilb
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            (the invertible isometries) are unitary.
          .un_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              A morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              in a †-category is called a
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/self-adjoint+morphism"} self-adjoint morphism
              if it equals its †-adjoint
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo †
                    %mo =
                    %mi f
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f^\dagger = f
                    \\,.
          %h3#CatOfDagCats The category of †-categories
          .un_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              Given two
              = succeed "-categories" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo †
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \dagger
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dagger+functor"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo †
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \dagger
                \-functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : A \to B
              consists of a function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mn 0
                    %mo :
                    %mi Ob
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Ob
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_0 : Ob(A) \to Ob(B)
              with a function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi F
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_{a,b}:Hom_A(a,b) \to Hom_B(F a,F b)
              for every object
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo :
                      %mi Ob
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a,b:Ob(A)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_{a,b}
              is generally also denoted as
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            %ul
              %li
                for every object
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi Ob
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in Ob(A)
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mn 1
                          %mi a
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mn 1
                          %mrow
                            %mi F
                            %mi a
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(1_a)=1_{F a}
              %li
                for every object
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo ,
                      %mi c
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Ob
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a,b,c \in Ob(A)
                and morphisms
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi Hom
                        %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \in Hom_A(a,b)
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi Hom
                          %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi b
                        %mo ,
                        %mi c
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \in Hom_A(b,c)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi g
                      %msub
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi A
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi F
                      %mi g
                      %msub
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi B
                      %mi F
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(g \circ_A f) = F g \circ_B F f
              %li
                for every object
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Ob
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a,b \in Ob(A)
                and morphism
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi Hom
                          %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \in Hom_A(a,b)
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi f
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mo †
                              %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi F
                        %mi f
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mo †
                              %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(f^{\dagger_A}) = (F f)^{\dagger_B}
          %p
            More concisely, one can say that a
            = succeed "-functor" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo †
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \dagger
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mo †
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ‡
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A,\dagger) \to (B,\ddagger)
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : A \to B
            of the underlying categories that commutes with the
            = succeed "-structures" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo †
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \dagger
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∘
                    %mo †
                    %mo =
                    %mo ‡
                    %mo ∘
                    %msup
                      %mi F
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \circ \dagger = \ddagger \circ F^{op}
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principle+of+equivalence"} principle of equivalence
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo †
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \dagger
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ‡
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ddagger
            are known to be the identity on objects (whatever that means), the two functors
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo ∘
                  %mo †
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\circ \dagger
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ‡
                  %mo ∘
                  %msup
                    %mi F
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ddagger \circ F^{op}
            automatically agree on objects.
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
            between
            = succeed "-functors" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo †
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \dagger
          .un_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              The †-adjoint
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi η
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta^*
              of a natural transformation
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                    %mo :
                    %mi F
                    %mo →
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\eta : F \to G
            %p
              between two †-functors
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo ,
                    %mi G
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mo †
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi D
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ‡
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F, G : (C,\dagger) \to (D,\ddagger)
              is given by the componentwise
              = succeed "-adjoint:" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ‡
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ddagger
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi η
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi a
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mi a
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ‡
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\eta^*)_a := (\eta_a)^\ddagger
                    \\,.
          %p
            To check that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi η
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta^*
            is indeed a natural transformation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi η
                    %mo *
                  %mo :
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta^* : G \to F
            consider
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi a
                  %mo →
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : a \to b
            any morphism in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo †
                  %mo :
                  %mi b
                  %mo →
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^\dagger : b \to a
            its
            = succeed "-adjoint" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo †
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \dagger
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi F
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi a
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi η
                                %mi a
                        %mtd
                          %mi G
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi a
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %mi F
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msup
                                  %mi f
                                  %mo †
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %mi G
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msup
                                  %mi f
                                  %mo †
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi F
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi b
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi η
                                %mi b
                        %mtd
                          %mi G
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi b
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  F(a) &amp;\stackrel{\eta_a}{\to}&amp; G(a)
                  \\\
                  \\uparrow^{\mathrlap{F(f^\dagger)}} &amp;&amp; \uparrow^{\mathrlap{G(f^\dagger)}}
                  \\\
                  F(b) &amp;\stackrel{\eta_b}{\to}&amp; G(b)
                  }
          %p
            be the corresponding naturality square of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta
            = succeed "-adjoint" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ‡
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ddagger
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi F
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi a
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ←
                            %mrow
                              %msubsup
                                %mi η
