          %p
            %br/
          %h2#References References
          %h3#general General
          %p
            Motivated by the example of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite-dimensional+Hilbert+spaces"} finite-dimensional Hilbert spaces
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo †
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \dagger
            %em strongly compact closed categories
            in
          %ul
            %li#AbramskyCoecke04
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Samson+Abramsky"}> Samson Abramsky
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bob+Coecke"} Bob Coecke
              = succeed "," do
                %em A categorical semantics of quantum protocols
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/quant-ph/0402130"} arXiv:quant-ph/0402130
          %p
            then named
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dagger+compact+closed+categories"} dagger compact closed categories
            in
          %ul
            %li#Selinger07
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Selinger"}> Peter Selinger
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Dagger compact closed categories and completely positive maps
              %strong 170
              (2007) 139-163 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.entcs.2006.12.018"}> doi:10.1016/j.entcs.2006.12.018
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.mscs.dal.ca/~selinger/papers.html#dagger"} web
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.mscs.dal.ca/~selinger/papers/dagger.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            and as such became the foundation of
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+information+theory+via+dagger-compact+categories"} quantum information theory via dagger-compact categories
          %p
            Exposition in this context of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+physics"} quantum physics
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"}> John Baez
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  The
                  = succeed "-category" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo ⋆
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \star
              = succeed "," do
                %em Quantum quandaries: a category-theoretic perspective
              = succeed "," do
                %em Structural Foundations of Quantum Gravity
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://math.ucr.edu/home/baez/quantum/node3.html"} web
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/quant-ph/0404040"} arXiv:quant-ph/0404040
          %p
            and of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+information+theory+via+dagger-compact+categories"} quantum information theory via dagger-compact categories
          %ul
            %li#HeunenVicary19
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Heunen"}> Chris Heunen
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jamie+Vicary"} Jamie Vicary
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Categories for Quantum Theory
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://global.oup.com/academic/product/categories-for-quantum-theory-9780198739616"} ISBN:9780198739616
              %p based on:
              %p#HeunenVicary12
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Heunen"}> Chris Heunen
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jamie+Vicary"} Jamie Vicary
                %em Lectures on categorical quantum mechanics
                (2012) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://www.cs.ox.ac.uk/files/4551/cqm-notes.pdf"}> pdf
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/HeunenVicary-QuantumLectures.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            But the notion of plain dagger categories has been considered much earlier, reinvented many times under different names (see
            %a{:href => "#Karvonen18"} Karvonen 2018 §1.2
            for more historical references) such as under the name “categories with involution”:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Saunders+Mac+Lane"}> Saunders Mac Lane
                , pp. 1045 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em An Algebra of Additive Relations
                %strong 47
                7 (1961) 1043-1051 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/71127"}> jstor:71127
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dieter+Puppe"}> Dieter Puppe
                , §1 in
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Korrespondenzen in abelschen Kategorien
                %strong 148
                (1962) 1–30 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01438388"}> doi:10.1007/BF01438388
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#Burgin70
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mark+S.+Burgin"}> Mark S. Burgin
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Categories with involution, and correspondences in
                    = succeed "-categories" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi γ
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma
                %strong 22
                (1970) 161–228 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://www.mathnet.ru/eng/mmo235"}> mathnet:mmo235
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Vaguely related is the notion of “symmetric category” is (analogous to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+proset"} symmetric proset
            or
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+bicategory"} symmetric bicategory
          %ul
            %li#Walters81
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+Walters"}> Robert Walters
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Sheaves and Cauchy complete categories
              %strong 22
              3 (1981) 283-286 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item?id=CTGDC_1981__22_3_283_0"}> numdam:CTGDC_1981__22_3_283_0
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p Still, dedicated discussion of these notions only appears later under the name of dagger-categories:
          %ul
            %li#Karvonen18
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martti+Karvonen"}> Martti Karvonen
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The Way of the Dagger
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1904.10805"} arXiv:1904.10805
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://mysite.science.uottawa.ca/mkarvone/papers/Karvonen%20-%20Thesis.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            concerning
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits"} limits
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Heunen"}> Chris Heunen
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martti+Karvonen"} Martti Karvonen
              = succeed "," do
                %em Limits in dagger categories
              %strong 34
              18 (2019) 468-513 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1803.06651"}> arXiv:1803.06651
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/34/18/34-18abs.html"} 34-18
          %p
            concerning
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monads"} monads
            (such as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frobenius+monad"} Frobenius
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+reader+monad"} quantum reader monad
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Heunen"}> Chris Heunen
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martti+Karvonen"} Martti Karvonen
              = succeed "," do
                %em Monads on dagger categories
              %strong 31
              35 (2016) 1016-1043 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1602.04324"}> arXiv:1602.04324
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/31/35/31-35abs.html"} tac:31-35
          %p concerning abstract characterization:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Luuk+Stehouwer"}> Luuk Stehouwer
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jan+Steinebrunner"} Jan Steinebrunner
              %em Dagger categories via anti-involutions and positivity
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2304.02928"}> arXiv:2304.02928
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Certain specially nice
            = succeed "-categories," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo †
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \dagger
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C-star-category"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi \
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\*
              \-categories
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+tensor+categories"} modular tensor categories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+quantum+field+theory"} topological quantum field theory
            and the theory of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+groups"} quantum groups
          %h3#ReferencesHigherDagger Higher dagger categories
          %p
            On dagger
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+categories"} higher categories
          %h4#dagger_1categories Dagger (∞,1)-categories
          %p
            Three definitions of dagger
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-categories"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              \-categories
            have been proposed by:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Simon+Henry"}> Simon Henry
              ,
              %em
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n,1)
                \-dagger categories
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://mathoverflow.net/a/427322/381"}> MO:a/427322
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            On
            = succeed "-presentations" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} objects
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-Grpd"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                    %mi Grpd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty Grpd
            by involutive
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+Segal+spaces"} complete Segal spaces
            are discussed (cf. the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Bergner12Erratum"} erratum
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Julia+Bergner"}> Julia Bergner
                \:
              %p
                %em> Adding inverses to diagrams encoding algebraic structures
                , Homology, Homotopy and Applications
                %strong 10
                2 (2008) 149-174 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://dx.doi.org/10.4310/HHA.2008.v10.n2.a8"}> doi:10.4310/HHA.2008.v10.n2.a8
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0610291"} arXiv:0610291
              %p
                %em> Adding inverses to diagrams II: Invertible homotopy theories are spaces
                , Homology, Homotopy and Applications
                %strong 10
                2 (2008) 175-193 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://dx.doi.org/10.4310/HHA.2008.v10.n2.a9"}> doi:10.4310/HHA.2008.v10.n2.a9
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0710.2254"} arXiv:0710.2254
              %p#Bergner12Erratum
                %em> Erratum to “Adding inverses to diagrams encoding algebraic structures” and “Adding inverses to diagrams II: Invertible homotopy theories are spaces”
                , Homology, Homotopy and Applications
                %strong 14
                1 (2012) 287-291 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://dx.doi.org/10.4310/HHA.2012.v14.n1.a15"}> doi:10.4310/HHA.2012.v14.n1.a15
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/pdf/0710.2254#page=18"} arXiv:0710.2254 pp 18
          %h4#dagger_ncategories Dagger (∞,n)-categories
          %p
            Generalization to dagger
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2Cn%29-categories"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,n)
                \-categories
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Theo+Johnson-Freyd"}> Theo Johnson-Freyd
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Dagger Higher Categories
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://categorified.net/dagger2023.html"} web
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Theo+Johnson-Freyd"}> Theo Johnson-Freyd
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Higher Dagger Categories
                %a{:href => "Center+for+Quantum+and+Topological+Systems#JohnsonFreydNov2023"} talk at
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CQTS"} CQTS
                (08 Nov 2023) &amp;lbrack;slides:
                %a{:href => "http://categorified.net/NYUADtalk.pdf"}> pdf
                ,
                = succeed "," do
